     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Blocking the single step h2_0:reach makes the target unreachable, and no smaller defense exists. crown:obtain is an OR of h5_0:pivot, h5_2:traverse and h5_1:obtain, so all three must be cut. h2_0:reach is a direct parent of h3_0:traverse (AND), h3_2:traverse (AND) and h3_1:access (OR with h2_0 as its only parent). Blocking h2_0 therefore kills all three. h5_0 (AND, needs h3_1 and h3_0) then dies. h5_2 (OR, only parent h3_2) dies. h4_1 (AND, needs h3_0, h3_2 and h2_0) dies, so h5_1 (AND, needs h4_1 and h3_1) dies too. The minimum is at least 1 because the target is reachable when nothing is blocked: h1_0, h1_2 and h2_0 are reachable from the footholds, giving h3_0, then h3_1, then h5_0, then crown.\"}"
    }
